        "content": "<p>This is some incredibly basic thing that I can't seem to find so I must be missing something, right?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Equiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm_trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 596266434,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779219003
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Huh. Yeah it's strange that we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=PartialEquiv.trans_symm_eq_symm_trans_symm#doc\">docs#PartialEquiv.trans_symm_eq_symm_trans_symm</a> for <code>PartialEquiv</code> but not for <code>Equiv</code>. Feels like an API gap to me.</p>",
        "id": 596271028,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1779220277
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you're adding this, can you do it for <code>EquivLike</code> perhaps?</p>",
        "id": 596272236,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779220584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think <code>EquivLike</code> has a <code>trans</code></p>",
        "id": 596272324,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779220602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39591\">#39591</a></p>",
        "id": 596272644,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779220697
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, <code>EquivLike</code> can't have an automatic <code>symm</code> or <code>trans</code> because you don't know whether your class is closed under any of these operations (think of <code>FunLike</code> classes like subsets of function spaces - <code>FunLike</code> only asserts properties about an individual element, not the collection).<br>\nI think something similar to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37779\">#37779</a> could work (but is even more work): you deprecate <code>Equiv.symm</code>in favour of the typeclasses <code>Symm</code> and <code>Trans</code>, and then you define a <code>IsSymmApply</code> class that says that <code>Symm.symm f x = y iff f y = x</code> or something along those lines. For <code>trans</code> it would be <code>Trans.trans f g x = f (g x)</code> in the above PR. However, I haven't thought about whether <code>EquivLike</code> has some subtle behaviour that makes this impossible (and also haven't thought about whether something in <code>Trans</code> or <code>Symm</code> would cause problems)..</p>",
        "id": 596299589,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1779229627
    }
]